(*
expect:
no rtc nil
still ringing
finished
*)
(* tuvm#100 — a board with no RTC answers nil, and the node must read that as
   "keep free-running", not as an error.

   There is deliberately NO env: header here. Unlike OEVM_NO_BELL / OEVM_NO_NTP,
   this seam needs no forcing knob to reach its structural-failure branch: a host
   genuinely has no DS3231, so ABSENCE IS THE DEFAULT (src/platform.c). 01 is the
   test that has to opt in, not this one. That asymmetry is worth stating, because
   it means the no-RTC path is exercised by every host run of this seam rather
   than only when someone remembers to set a variable.

   The second line is the actual claim, and it is 06_ntp_nosync's claim about the
   other timebase. Answering nil is only half the contract; the other half is that
   nil is an ORDINARY answer, so a node can branch on it with no handler in sight.
   If this seam ever grows a raise, this test stops reaching `still ringing` — the
   intended alarm, because the failure would otherwise surface as a clock that
   stops ringing when the RTC is unplugged, the exact opposite of what the seam
   promises. A ship's bell whose battery-backed clock fails should fall back to
   free-running, not fall silent.

   The `secs == nil` test is doing real work rather than restating the seam: the
   failing form of this test (verified by temporarily making the host answer 0)
   prints `rtc unexpectedly answered: 0`, and ZERO IS A VALID READING — 0 seconds
   since local midnight is exactly midnight, the moment the day's first strike is
   due. So "no clock" and "the top of the day" must not collapse to the same
   answer, and only nil-vs-SMI keeps them apart. A seam that signalled absence
   with a sentinel 0 would silently strike eight bells every time the RTC was
   unplugged. *)
class WallClockAbsent packageUsing: manifest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | secs |
    secs:: platform wallClock.
    secs == nil
      ifTrue:  [ 'no rtc nil' out ]
      ifFalse: [ ('rtc unexpectedly answered: ' , secs printString) out ].

    (* No handler anywhere above or below: reaching this line at all is the proof
       that a missing RTC is an answer and not a raise. *)
    'still ringing' out.
    'finished' out.
  )
) : (
)
